30.2(1)(A) (A) analysis of the Person's daily work tasks that will help to teach, train, and provide instructions to the Person to independently complete as many of the tasks as possible;
30.2(1)(B) (B) on-site monitoring and training, or retraining, as needed, for specific job tasks, with the primary goal of reducing the need for support and promoting independence. Training and instruction may include: (i) instructional prompts; (ii) verbal and written instructions; (iii) self-management tools; (iv) role play; (v) modeling and (vi) fading of supports;
30.2(1)(C) (C) personal assistance with ADL. Although personal assistance may be a component of SEI support, it may not comprise the entirety of the service;
30.2(1)(D) (D) supervision of the Person to ensure the Person's health and safety. Employment supervision must not be provided as a part of SEI;
30.2(1)(E) (E) direct job support, as needed, to the Person via teleservices to fade paid supports and promote on-the-job independence. Direct job support that is essential for the Person's successful employment must be provided while the Person is on the job. That Contractor shall not provide support via teleservices for the convenience of the Contactor or other members of the team. Teleservices support must be combined with in-person support;
30.2(1)(F) (F) assistance and training on employment related communication, including: (i) schedules and time management; (ii) accommodations and assistive technology; (iii) self-advocacy; (iv) how to interact with supervisors, co-workers, customers and others; (v) work culture; and (vi) employment goals and performance;
30.2(1)(G) (G) advising or discussing with the Person or others any aspect of the processes of obtaining and maintaining employment; and
30.2(1)(H) (H) developing and implementing guidelines for conduct in line with employer expectations and resolving any workplace problems.

30.3(4)(A) (A) the Person's name;
30.3(4)(B) (B) the service provider to the Person (SEI);
30.3(4)(C) (C) date range the summary covers;
30.3(4)(D) (D) details of all employment activities;
30.3(4)(E) (E) the person's response to the services;
30.3(4)(F) (F) information that indicates the progress towards the Person's employment goals; and
30.3(4)(G) (G) name of the Staff writing the monthly summary.

31.2(1)(B) (B) homemaker skills building;
31.2(1)(C) (C) advocacy and self-help;
31.2(1)(D) (D) accessing the community, communication, and socialization;
31.2(1)(E) (E) personal finances including keeping track of money and bills; and
31.2(1)(F) (F) accessing community services.

31.3(3)(A) (A) the inventory completion date and the Staff's name that completed the inventory;
31.3(3)(B) (B) belongings that have significant value to the Person;
31.3(3)(C) (C) belongings with a purchase value of $50.00 or more;
31.3(3)(D) (D) all new items added as received by the Person that have significant value to the Person or with a purchase value of $50.00 or more; and
31.3(3)(E) (E) discarded items must be removed, including the reason for discard and signature from the Person or their legal guardian.

32.2(1)(B) (B) homemaker skills building;
32.2(1)(C) (C) advocacy and self-help;
32.2(1)(D) (D) accessing the community, communication and socialization;
32.2(1)(E) (E) personal finances including keeping track of money and bills; and
32.2(1)(F) (F) accessing community services.

32.3(2)(A) (A) the Person's name;
32.3(2)(B) (B) the service provided to the Person (CMP or CMS);
32.3(2)(C) (C) date range the monthly summary covers;
32.3(2)(D) (D) general summary of the service provided, the Person's status and response to the service, and notable events and activities related to the service;
32.3(2)(E) (E) information that indicates the progress towards the Person's goals; and
32.3(2)(F) (F) the name of the Staff writing the monthly summary.

33.2(d)(1) (1) a summary of the Discovery Process;
33.2(d)(2) (2) recommendations for the Person's employment goals; and
33.2(d)(3) (3) strategies to be used in obtaining Customized Employment.

33.2(e)(1) (1) the Person's existing skills and interests that can be transferred into successful Competitive Integrated Employment;
33.2(e)(2) (2) the Person's strengths and where they need support;
33.2(e)(3) (3) the Person's learning strategies; and
33.2(e)(4) (4) needed accommodations for the worksite.

33.2(f)(1) (1) identifying potential employers and job opportunities in the community that match the Person's employment goals;
33.2(f)(2) (2) supporting the Person in networking with potential employers as identified in either the Individualized Strengths-based Job Discovery Assessment or Vocational Assessment; and
33.2(f)(3) (3) explaining potential job details to the Person.

33.2(g)(1) (1) job site and analysis, including having Staff visit potential community employment sites to identify job tasks or workflow implementations that may create job task opportunities for the Person;
33.2(g)(2) (2) job shadowing or informational interview, including having Staff visit potential community employment sites to coordinate job shadowing or informational interviews or experiences that provide the Person with a realistic view of job tasks;
33.2(g)(3) (3) paid community-integrated internships or temporary seasonal work experiences;
33.2(g)(4) (4) work-based learning opportunities;
33.2(g)(5) (5) mock interviews; and
33.2(g)(6) (6) visits to local businesses to learn about different companies, products, services, or employment opportunities.

33.2(h)(1) (1) how to obtain and retain employment;
33.2(h)(2) (2) job searching;
33.2(h)(3) (3) filling out applications and creating resumes and letters for employment;
33.2(h)(4) (4) marketing the Person's skills to potential employers;
33.2(h)(5) (5) job related time management;
33.2(h)(6) (6) technology skills related to job searching and retainment;
33.2(h)(7) (7) what workplace accommodations are needed and how to request them;
33.2(h)(8) (8) self-advocacy and when or how to disclose a disability;
33.2(h)(9) (9) work cultures and how to interact with supervisors, co-workers, and customers;
33.2(h)(10) (10) setting employment goals and using person-centered planning tools;
33.2(h)(12) (12) skill building and assistance to the Person with their ADLs (assistance with ADLs may be a component of SJD, but it may not comprise the entirety of the service).

33.2(m)(1) (1) onboarding and required employer training;
33.2(m)(2) (2) assessment of the employment setting to evaluate task management, core job skill requirements, identification of the needed skills, and social support necessary for the Person to be successful;
33.2(m)(3) (3) coordinating with the Person and the employer to develop written details of job duties, expectations, and how to resolve workplace problems;
33.2(m)(4) (4) assessment of the employment setting for needed accommodations, including:
33.2(m)(4)(A) (A) identifying reasonable work site accommodations and accessibility needed for the Person to retain or enhance their employment; and
33.2(m)(4)(B) (B) coordinating with the employer, USOR Vocational Rehabilitation Services, the Person's DSPD support coordinator, and providing support to the Person to ensure the Person receives needed accommodations and accessibility that are legally required;
33.2(m)(5) (5) developing skills to independently access transportation to and from their employment site;
33.2(m)(6) (6) with the Person's informed consent and preferred level of disclosure, encouraging and providing skill building to the Person and the Person's co-workers, supervisors, and other employer contacts on engagement of natural co-worker support to the Person that is not specifically compensated, with the goal to minimize or eliminate the need for the Person to have continued paid supports; and
33.2(m)(7) (7) coordinating with and providing employment information to other individuals involved in the Person's employment goals.
